# The documents set source at 80 columns and never break a line, so an
# example wider than that overflows its frame. //:fmt_test checks the
# crates but not this package, which is the one place the width is
# load bearing (issue 281), so the check lives here, beside the list it
# reads. Every one of those files is a target of its own named after
# it; the three foreign wrappers have no Rust source and are not here.
rustfmt_test(
    name = "fmt_test",
    targets = [":" + s[:-3] for s in SOURCES if s.endswith(".rs")],
)
